sn22.79:12.1 | S: This is called a noble disciple who gets rid of and doesn’t accumulate; | T: “This, monks, is called a disciple of the noble ones who tears down and does not build up;
sn22.79:12.2 | S: who gives up and doesn’t grasp; | T: who abandons and does not cling;
sn22.79:12.3 | S: who unmeshes and doesn’t enmesh; | T: who discards and does not pull in;
sn22.79:12.4 | S: who dissipates and doesn’t get clouded. | T: who scatters and does not pile up.
sn22.79:12.5 | S: And what things do they get rid of and not accumulate? | T: “And what does he tear down and not build up?
sn22.79:12.6 | S: They get rid of form and don’t accumulate it. | T: He tears down form and does not build it up.

